{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalPoint","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalPoint","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Category.Basic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalPoint.point","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalPoint.point","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-point.lean#L34-L34","doc":"The point morphism `p : 𝟙 → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalPoint.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalPoint.mk","kind":"ctor","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-point.lean#L31-L31","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalPoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalPoint","kind":"structure","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-point.lean#L21-L34","doc":"**Categorical point** of a Frobenius–Hopf object.\n\nA morphism `p : 𝟙 → A` in a monoidal category `C`.  In the archimedean\nrealisation `A = 𝒪(G)`, a point corresponds to evaluation at `g ∈ G`;\nfor `A = C^∞(M)`, to a point of the manifold `M`.\n\nThe augmentation ideal at `p` is `𝔪_p = ker(p* : A → 𝟙)`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:categorical-point}`\nRef: [kock2004] https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511615443 ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:categorical-point","label":"def:categorical-point","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-point.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}